  <StandardBlock
  sectionID="why-this-matters"
    alignText="left"
    alignBody="right"
    imageAlt="Image"
    imageSrc={pholder}
    textMarkdown=`## Why **Malue** exists
Healthcare does not lack intelligence. It often lacks the infrastructure to capture that intelligence, structure it, compare it, act on it and scale it. Healthcare professionals know where waste happens. Patients experience the consequences of design decisions. Procurement teams understand the difficulty of complex choices. Industry partners often know where innovation can help, but need credible real-world evidence to support adoption.  
Malue is being built to bring these perspectives together and help healthcare systems make better decisions and adopt better ways of working.  
### From waste to adoption
Malue began with a focus on operational waste in healthcare. That focus quickly revealed a deeper challenge: even when better ideas, products or practices exist, healthcare systems often struggle to adopt them. The problem is not only innovation. It is adoption. Malue's platform has therefore been designed to support the movement from insight to implementation, and from implementation to measurable impact.
### Built through research and validation
Malue's development has been shaped by years of research, stakeholder engagement and functional validation across broad healthcare themes including product and service evaluation, procurement decision support, professional engagement, sustainability, post-market feedback, pathway adoption, operational improvement, contribution recognition and innovation adoption. This work has moved Malue beyond concept and into a validated pre-market stage.
### A mission-led commercial model
Malue is designed to create commercial value and social value together. The company purpose is to help healthcare systems use resources more intelligently, improve adoption of valuable innovation, reduce waste, support sustainability and recognise the people whose work creates improvement. As Malue matures commercially, the company aims to reinvest a portion of value into healthcare improvement activity aligned with its mission.`
  />

